    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Your dracoleum lingers long after its been discharged and expelled from your body. A creature who fails or critically fails its saving throw takes </span>@Damage[2d6[persistent,@actor.flags.system.drachiriBenefactor.damageType]]<span> </span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">persistent damage of the same type. On a critical failure, the flat check to remove the persistent damage increases to DC 20 (or DC 15 if they have appropriate help to remove it). If you apply a critical weapon specialization effect that also deals the same type of persistent damage, apply this persistent damage in addition to the base persistent damage.</span></p>"
